#: ../../source/reference/configuration/cmd_args.md:28
msgid "Rules of the command line"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/cmd_args.md:29
msgid ""
"**An absent flag leaves its option unset, never set to a default.** "
"Defaults belong to the defaults tier, and a command line that set "
"everything would make every other source unreachable — a configuration "
"file could then never contribute anything."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/cmd_args.md:33
msgid ""
"The visible consequence is that the three boolean flags can only be "
"switched **on** here. `--archive` absent means *nothing said*, not false."
" To say false, use a source that can spell it: `FREEPORTS_ARCHIVE=false`,"
" or `archive: false`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/cmd_args.md:37
msgid ""
"**`-v` and `-q` are independent dials**, not opposed flags. Both are "
"counted, the net offset `verbose - quiet` is added to the default and "
"clamped, and using them together is never an error. The option is left "
"unset unless at least one of the two appears."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/cmd_args.md:41
msgid ""
"**Repeatable flags leave the option unset when absent**, not empty. `-i` "
"given zero times is not \"no documents\", it is \"this source says "
"nothing about documents\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/cmd_args.md:44
msgid "What the command line rejects outright"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/cmd_args.md:45
msgid ""
"Three things are rejected here rather than later, each with the flag's "
"own name in the message so that someone who mistyped `--pages` reads "
"`--pages` and not a generic sentence about parallelism:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/cmd_args.md:48
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"a document specifier that does not parse "
"({doc}`../../guides/user/documents`);"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/cmd_args.md:49
msgid ""
"a parallelism value that is not a positive integer or `auto` — including "
"zero and negatives, which is why hyphen values have to be accepted at "
"all: without that, `-1` would be taken for an unknown option and the "
"typed error could never be reached;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/cmd_args.md:52
msgid "an output profile that is not one of the three names."
msgstr ""

